/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  phaseSplit01_freeze_water_ethanol -- THE PHASE SPLIT ALONG T (DEV.md 4c C118).

  The same liquor flash21 freezes at ONE temperature (-15 C), cooled here from
  0 to -20 C one kelvin at a time: at every grid point ONE isothermal flash,
  the flash21 unit's own solver (IsothermalFlash::solveCore), under flash21's
  own sealed records -- water, ethanol, the curated NRTL pair, the C3
  `phases ( liquor liquid; ice solid crystallizing )` declaration.  Nothing
  is re-derived; the point at 258.15 K IS flash21's answer (the gate holds it
  to flash21's golden).

  WHAT A STUDENT WATCHES.  Above the liquor's freezing point the feed is one
  liquid and the declared ice stays subsaturated: the water activity gamma_w
  x_w (0.917) sits BELOW the saturation value exp(-dG_fus/RT) the crystal
  would need (1 at the triple point, falling as T falls).  Between -8 and
  -9 C the two cross, ice APPEARS (announced, between the two grid values it
  lies between), and from there down the liquor concentrates exactly along
  the freezing-point-depression identity

      gamma_w * x_w  =  exp(-dHfus (1 - T/Tt) / (R T))

  with every quantity from the record's own data (Hfus 6008 J/mol, triple
  point 273.16 K) -- published at every point as `a_water` beside
  `aEq_water`, equal to round-off wherever ice is present, and recomputed
  independently by check_phase_split_scan.  By -20 C nearly 60 % of the feed
  is ice and the liquor is about a quarter ethanol.

  NOT MODELLED, said plainly (the run says it too): nucleation and
  supercooling -- every point is the equilibrium ceiling; an ethanol solid
  or a eutectic -- no record declares one, so the liquor never solidifies
  completely in this model; solute inclusion in the ice; the liquid/solid
  heat-capacity term of dG_fus (announced by the record, |T - Tt| up to
  20 K here).  Every sub-273 K vapour pressure is an announced extrapolation
  of the Antoine fit (it cancels in the SLE identity: both phases share one
  Psat), and the NRTL pair is used below its fitted window (announced).  No
  number here is anchored to a measured freezing-point datum: a STRUCTURAL
  witness, like flash21.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
operations
(
    {
        name      freeze;
        type      phaseSplitScan;

        //  The HELD axis and the feed (moles).  The swept axis lives in
        //  `vary` only -- declaring T here too is refused by name.
        state
        {
            P            1.0 atm;
            composition  { water 0.9;  ethanol 0.1; }
        }

        //  0 -> -20 C, one kelvin per point (21 points, descending: a
        //  cooling scan reads top-down as the freezer would run it).
        vary
        {
            variable  T;
            from      273.15 K;
            to        253.15 K;
            n         21;
        }

        output    { file freeze.csv; }
    }
);
